<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John the Exarch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 900</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John the Exarch was a Bulgarian scholar and churchman of the late 9th and early 10th centuries, active at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/preslav">Preslav</a> under Simeon I. His Hexaemeron, a commentary on the six days of creation drawn from Greek sources, includes a celebrated description of Simeon's court. He also translated part of John of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>'s Source of Knowledge, helping to create a Slavonic theological vocabulary.</p></div>
